OL,3,AEU announces plan to restrict social
OL,4,Amedia access for children
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe EU has announced plans to restrict
OL,7,Fsocial media access for under-16s
OL,8,Facross its member states, in a bid to
OL,9,Fincrease wellbeing and tackle online
OL,10,Fsafety.
OL,12,FUnder the plans, there would be a
OL,13,Fgradual approach to children using
OL,14,Fsocial media which would include
OL,15,Fbanning under 13s from accessing
OL,16,Fplatforms.
OL,18,FThose aged 13 to 15 would only be able
OL,19,Fto access platforms for an hour per day
OL,20,Fvia "mini accounts" set up through
OL,21,Ftheir parent or guardian's social media
OL,22,Faccount.
OL,23,APub: 17-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,315,300,200,140,0,100
